{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":26205705,"ns":0,"title":"Open texture","extract":"Open texture is a term in the philosophy of Friedrich Waismann, first introduced in his paper \"Verifiability\" to refer to the universal possibility of vagueness in empirical statements. He had coined the phrase \"die Porosität der Begriffe\" (\"the porosity of concepts\") for this purpose and credits William Kneale for suggesting the English term that he then adopted.","description":"Philosophical term introduced by Friedrich Waismann","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}